add(26,
'The bar chart compares female unemployment rates in England, Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland in 2013 and 2014.',
'Overall, unemployment among women fell in three of the four countries, with Scotland being the only exception. England had the highest rate in 2013, but Scotland recorded the highest figure in 2014. Northern Ireland experienced the largest decline.',
'In England, the female unemployment rate decreased slightly from 6.8% in 2013 to 6.5% in 2014. Despite this fall, the figure remained above those for Wales and Northern Ireland. Scotland followed the opposite pattern, with its rate rising from 6.1% to 6.7%. This increase of 0.6 percentage points meant that Scotland moved ahead of England by the second year.',
'The rates in the other two countries were lower. In Wales, unemployment among women fell from 5.4% to 5%, a reduction of 0.4 percentage points. Northern Ireland saw a larger drop, from 5.6% in 2013 to 4.6% in 2014. It therefore changed from having a slightly higher rate than Wales to having the lowest rate among all four countries.',
'Chỉ Scotland tăng; Northern Ireland giảm nhiều nhất (1 điểm phần trăm). Hai mốc không chứng minh xu hướng liên tục.',
'Body 1: England–Scotland cao hơn. Body 2: Wales–Northern Ireland.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','compare'],{'years':[2013,2014],'unit':'percent','England':[6.8,6.5],'Wales':[5.4,5.0],'Scotland':[6.1,6.7],'Northern Ireland':[5.6,4.6]})
add(27,
'The diagram shows the stages involved in manufacturing ceramic pots, from obtaining raw materials to producing the finished items.',
'Overall, the process includes preparing and shaping the material, followed by drying, heating and colouring. The pots are heated twice, with colour being added between the two heating stages.',
'First, raw materials are dug out of the ground using a machine. They are loaded onto a truck and transported to the factory. At the factory, the materials are crushed and then mixed. The mixture is placed into moulds to give it the required shape. It is left to dry for four to six hours before the clay pots are assembled and removed for further processing.',
'Next, the assembled pots are put into an oven and heated at 1,000 degrees Celsius. After this stage, they are dipped into colour, as shown by a pot being lowered into a container. The coloured pots then undergo another heating stage, labelled colour firing in the diagram. At the end of this final stage, the ceramic pots are complete and ready as finished products.',
'Đi theo mũi tên: raw materials → crushing/mixing → moulds/drying → assembly → oven → colour → colour firing. Không thêm thời lượng nung.',
'Body 1: nguyên liệu và tạo hình. Body 2: nung, màu và thành phẩm.',['process-overview','process-order'],{'drying_hours':'4–6','oven_celsius':1000})
add(28,
'The line graph compares coffee exports from Brazil, Colombia and Costa Rica between 2002 and 2012, measured in millions of kilograms.',
'Overall, all three countries exported more coffee at the end than at the beginning. Brazil became the largest exporter, while Colombia showed the sharpest fluctuations and remained below the other two countries in 2012.',
'Brazil exported approximately 12 million kilograms in 2002. Its figure rose to about 15 million in 2006 and 20 million in 2008, before slipping to around 18 million in 2010. It then climbed to 25 million in 2012. Costa Rica started higher, at 15 million kilograms, but its exports fell to roughly 7 million in 2006. They subsequently recovered, reaching 20 million in the final year.',
'Colombia had the lowest initial figure, at 5 million kilograms. Exports increased to around 7 million in 2004 and 12 million in 2006, briefly exceeding Costa Rica. However, this was followed by a sharp fall to only 2 million in 2008. The figure then recovered to about 8 million in 2010 and 15 million in 2012, three times its starting level.',
'Brazil lớn nhất cuối kỳ; cả ba tăng đầu–cuối; Colombia có đáy sâu năm 2008. Đơn vị triệu kg.',
'Body 1: Brazil–Costa Rica. Body 2: Colombia nhiều biến động.',['intro','overview-trend','sequence','from-to'],{'years':[2002,2004,2006,2008,2010,2012],'unit':'million kg','approximate':True,'Brazil':[12,14,15,20,18,25],'Costa Rica':[15,10,7,12,14,20],'Colombia':[5,7,12,2,8,15]})
add(29,
'The table compares the average weekly salaries of men and women in five occupational groups in 2015, measured in dollars.',
'Overall, men earned more than women in every occupation. Professionals received the highest salaries for both sexes, while manual workers earned the least. The largest gap between men and women was among technicians.',
'Male professionals earned $2,000 per week, compared with $1,900 for female professionals. This difference of $100 was the smallest gap in the table. Technicians showed a much larger difference: the average for men was $1,400, whereas women received $900. The $500 gap in this group was five times the gap among professionals.',
'In administrative and clerical work, men earned $1,350 per week and women earned $1,000. Service workers had a similar difference of $350, with weekly salaries of $1,300 for men and $950 for women. Manual workers had the lowest pay in both groups, at $1,100 and $850 respectively. Thus, although the ranking of some occupations differed between men and women, the highest-paid and lowest-paid groups were the same.',
'Men cao hơn ở mọi nghề; professionals cao nhất và chênh ít nhất; technicians chênh nhiều nhất. Không suy luận nguyên nhân chênh lương.',
'Body 1: professionals và technicians. Body 2: ba nghề còn lại.',['intro','static-overview','compare','respectively'],{'unit':'dollars/week','occupations':['Technicians','Service workers','Professionals','Administrative/clerical workers','Manual workers'],'men':[1400,1300,2000,1350,1100],'women':[900,950,1900,1000,850]})
add(30,
'The maps show how the waterfront area of Darwin changed between 2009 and 2014.',
'Overall, industrial land was replaced by residential, educational and green areas. A harbour and an additional swimming pool were introduced, while several existing features, including the school, convention centre and lake, remained.',
'In 2009, industrial areas occupied much of the land below the main road and around the central lake. By 2014, these areas had been removed. More residential buildings had been added near the existing row of housing, and a university building had appeared to the left of the expanded residential area. Trees were planted across much of the lower part of the site, creating a greener landscape.',
'Several facilities were retained in the upper section, including the school and convention centre. The central lake and the trees near it also remained. A new swimming pool was built near the school, while the two existing pools beside the sea were kept. On the lower right, a harbour was added along the waterfront and connected to the area by a route. The fishing area remained on the far right.',
'Industrial land giảm, có university/housing/trees và harbour. Chỉ mô tả công trình thể hiện; không thêm số căn hộ.',
'Body 1: thay đổi khu công nghiệp và nhà ở. Body 2: công trình giữ lại và tiện ích ven biển.',['map-overview','map-change','location'])
add(31,
'The table compares underground railway systems in six cities in terms of opening date, route length and annual passenger numbers.',
'Overall, London has the oldest and longest system, while Tokyo carries the most passengers. Kyoto has both the shortest route and the lowest passenger figure, and Los Angeles has the newest system.',
'London’s railway opened in 1863 and has 394 kilometres of route, almost twice the length of the Paris system at 199 kilometres. Paris opened in 1900 and serves 1,191 million passengers per year, compared with 775 million in London. Tokyo, which opened in 1927, has a shorter route of 155 kilometres but the highest annual passenger total, at 1,927 million.',
'The remaining systems are smaller and less busy. Washington DC opened in 1976 and has 126 kilometres of route, carrying 144 million passengers annually. Kyoto began operating in 1981 and has only 11 kilometres of route, with 45 million passengers per year. Finally, the Los Angeles system opened in 2001. Its 28-kilometre route is longer than Kyoto’s, but its passenger total is only slightly higher, at 50 million.',
'Tách 3 tiêu chí: tuổi hệ thống, km tuyến và triệu lượt/năm. Không dùng ngày mở như chuỗi thời gian sản lượng.',
'Body 1: London–Paris–Tokyo. Body 2: Washington DC–Kyoto–Los Angeles.',['intro','static-overview','compare','respectively'],{'cities':['London','Paris','Tokyo','Washington DC','Kyoto','Los Angeles'],'opened':[1863,1900,1927,1976,1981,2001],'km':[394,199,155,126,11,28],'million_passengers_year':[775,1191,1927,144,45,50]})
add(32,
'The line graph compares the percentage of total energy generated from renewable sources in six countries between 2010 and 2013.',
'Overall, all six countries ended with higher percentages than they began with. Germany showed the greatest rise and became the leading country, while the USA remained at the bottom of the group throughout the period.',
'In 2010, China had the highest proportion, at approximately 19%, compared with about 17% in Germany. China’s figure fell to around 17% in 2011, before recovering to just over 20% in 2013. Germany followed a stronger upward trend, increasing to about 20% in 2011 and 25% at the end. India also rose overall, from roughly 17% to around 17.5%, after a small fall in the second year.',
'The other three countries recorded lower figures. Spain increased gradually from about 13% to approximately 15.5%, while France moved from around 12.5% to 15%. The USA started at roughly 10%, rose to about 12.5% in 2011, and then dipped slightly. By 2013, its proportion had recovered to around 13%, still below those of all the other countries.',
'Germany tăng mạnh nhất; USA thấp nhất. Số liệu đường được đọc xấp xỉ, không dùng quiz yêu cầu số thập phân chính xác.',
'Body 1: Germany, China, India. Body 2: Spain, France, USA.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','similar'])
add(33,
'The pie chart shows the nationalities of people living in Australia, while the table compares the percentages of five nationality groups living in cities and the countryside.',
'Overall, Australians made up by far the largest share of the population. All five groups were mainly urban, with Chinese residents showing the highest proportion living in cities.',
'Australians represented 73% of the population, followed by people of other nationalities at 14%. British people were the largest separately identified overseas group, accounting for 7%. New Zealanders made up 3%, while Chinese and Dutch residents represented smaller shares, at 2% and 1% respectively. The combined share of these three smaller groups was therefore below the British figure.',
'Turning to location, 99% of Chinese residents lived in cities, leaving only 1% in the countryside. The urban figures for New Zealanders and British residents were also high, at 90% and 89%. Dutch residents were slightly less concentrated in cities, with 83% living there and 17% in rural areas. Australians had the lowest urban proportion of the five groups, at 80%, and the largest countryside share, at 20%.',
'Pie là cơ cấu nationality; bảng là city/countryside trong từng nationality. Không trộn hai mẫu số.',
'Body 1: pie chart. Body 2: bảng nơi cư trú.',['intro','static-overview','compare','respectively'],{'population_percent':{'Australian':73,'British':7,'New Zealander':3,'Chinese':2,'Dutch':1,'Other':14},'city_percent':{'Australian':80,'British':89,'New Zealander':90,'Chinese':99,'Dutch':83}})
hold(34,'Câu hỏi nói lý do đi làm bằng xe đạp/ô tô nhưng hình là bảng chi tiêu gia đình. Bảng tương ứng với q075; dùng q075 thay vì học theo câu hỏi ghép nhầm.')
add(35,
'The line graph compares mobile and fixed-line telephone subscriptions in Africa between 1994 and 2004, measured per 100 inhabitants.',
'Overall, both types of subscription increased, but mobile use grew much faster. Fixed lines were more common at the beginning, whereas mobile subscriptions overtook them around 2001 and finished far ahead.',
'In 1994, there were approximately 1.7 fixed-line subscriptions per 100 inhabitants, compared with only 0.06 mobile subscriptions. The fixed-line figure increased slowly, reaching about 2 subscriptions in the late 1990s and around 2.5 by 2000. It then changed relatively little before rising to 3.1 per 100 inhabitants in 2004.',
'Mobile subscriptions remained below one per 100 inhabitants until the late 1990s. They then increased more quickly, reaching roughly 2 in 2000 and 3 in 2001, when they moved above fixed lines. This growth continued, with approximately 4.5 mobile subscriptions per 100 people in 2002 and 6 in 2003. By 2004, the figure had reached 8.8, nearly three times the fixed-line figure and far above its very low starting point.',
'Đơn vị subscriptions/100 inhabitants, không đồng nhất với phần trăm người sở hữu vì một người có thể có nhiều thuê bao. Trục bắt đầu 1994.',
'Body 1: fixed line tăng chậm. Body 2: mobile tăng mạnh và vượt.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','peak'],{'unit':'subscriptions per 100 inhabitants','years':[1994,2004],'fixed':[1.7,3.1],'mobile':[0.06,8.8]},'Chú thích dưới hình ghi 1995–2004 nhưng trục và lời đề bắt đầu 1994. Bài theo trục năm/lời đề; đã ghi rõ khác biệt.')
add(36,
'The diagram shows the process used to manufacture carbonated drinks, from cleaning water to delivering the finished products to supermarkets.',
'Overall, there are five main stages. Water is cleaned, heated and carbonated before other ingredients are mixed in. The drinks are then filtered, placed in containers and packaged for delivery.',
'In the first stage, raw water passes through a filter and is treated with a water softener and chemicals. A pump then moves the cleaned water to electric heaters. After heating, the water travels through a cooling pipe and enters a tank, where carbon dioxide is added. The resulting carbonated water flows down a pipe to the mixing stage.',
'Inside the mixing tank, colouring, syrup and flavour are added to the carbonated water. The mixture then passes through another filter before being put into two types of container: bottles and cans. These filled containers are packed into boxes during the final stage. The boxes are loaded onto a truck and transported to a supermarket, completing the process shown in the diagram.',
'Năm stage có nhãn rõ; hai lần lọc; CO₂ trước mixing. Không thêm mức nhiệt, tỷ lệ syrup hoặc thời gian.',
'Body 1: stages 1–2. Body 2: stages 3–5.',['process-overview','process-order'],{'stages':['cleaning','heating/cooling/carbonation','mixing','filtering and filling','packaging']})
add(37,
'The plans show changes to Happy Valley Shopping Centre between 1982 and 2012.',
'Overall, the shopping centre expanded into the surrounding area and gained a car park and themed restaurants. The lake disappeared, while the central entertainment area remained and several shops were moved or enlarged.',
'In 1982, a lake occupied the left-hand side of the site, with trees around much of the centre. The main shopping building was to the right of the lake, and its entrance faced left. Inside, the entertainment area was in the middle, surrounded by a coffee shop, a food store and several specialist shops. Toilets were near the lower-left corner of the building.',
'By 2012, the lake had been replaced by a furniture retail area, and a parking lot had been built below it. The entertainment area remained central, but the sports and electronics stores were now along the upper side. The food store had moved to the lower right, and themed restaurants occupied the right-hand side. The toilets remained near the entrance, while some trees were removed to make room for the larger development.',
'Lake → furniture retail; bãi đỗ phía dưới trái; entertainment giữ ở giữa; themed restaurants bên phải.',
'Body 1: bản 1982. Body 2: các thay đổi đến 2012.',['map-overview','map-change','location'])
add(38,
'The table compares poverty levels among different household types in Australia in 1999, giving both percentages and numbers of people.',
'Overall, sole-parent households had the highest poverty rate, while aged couples had the lowest. However, couples with children accounted for the largest number of people in poverty. Across all households, the overall rate was 11%.',
'Among sole-parent households, 21% of people lived in poverty, representing 232,000 individuals. Single people without children had the next highest rate, at 19%, or 359,000 people. The figure for couples with children was lower, at 12%, but the number affected was much greater, at 933,000. This was the largest total for any household type in the table.',
'The remaining groups had poverty rates below the national figure. Couples without children recorded 7%, equivalent to 211,000 people. For single aged people, the rate was 6%, with 54,000 affected. Aged couples had the lowest percentage, at 4%, and the smallest number, at 48,000. In total, 1,837,000 people across all household types were living in poverty in the year shown.',
'Phân biệt rate với số người: sole parent 21% cao nhất nhưng couple with children 933,000 nhiều nhất. Không cộng tỷ lệ các nhóm.',
'Body 1: ba nhóm tỷ lệ cao. Body 2: ba nhóm thấp và tổng.',['intro','static-overview','compare','respectively'],{'unit':'percent and people','sole parent':[21,232000],'single no children':[19,359000],'couple with children':[12,933000],'couple no children':[7,211000],'single aged':[6,54000],'aged couple':[4,48000],'all':[11,1837000]})
duplicate(39,38)
add(40,
'The bar chart compares the percentages of people with different levels of science qualification in Malaysia and Singapore.',
'Overall, having no science qualification was the most common situation in both countries. Singapore had a larger proportion of people with a bachelor’s degree, while Malaysia recorded higher shares for school-leaving qualifications and no science qualification.',
'Approximately 65% of people in Malaysia had no qualification in science, compared with about 60% in Singapore. These were by far the largest figures in the chart. School-leaving exams were the next most common level, accounting for roughly 35% in Malaysia and 30% in Singapore. Malaysia therefore exceeded Singapore by around five percentage points in each of these two categories.',
'The pattern was different for bachelor’s degrees. About 20% of people in Singapore held this qualification in science, twice the Malaysian figure of approximately 10%. Master’s degrees were much less common in both countries, with figures of around 3% each. Thus, although the countries had similar proportions at the highest qualification level shown, there was a clear difference in the share holding a first university degree.',
'So sánh từng cấp, không cộng các mức thành 100% vì biểu đồ không xác nhận nhóm loại trừ nhau. Master khoảng 3% ở cả hai.',
'Body 1: no qualification và school exams. Body 2: bachelor và master.',['intro','static-overview','compare'])
add(41,
'The line graph compares the production of paper and packaging, wood pulp and sawn wood in the UK between 1980 and 2000, in millions of tonnes.',
'Overall, paper and packaging had the highest output throughout and increased considerably. Sawn wood production declined, while wood pulp fell initially and then recovered slightly, ending below its starting level.',
'In 1980, paper and packaging production was approximately 230 million tonnes, compared with 200 million tonnes of sawn wood and about 170 million tonnes of wood pulp. Over the next ten years, the figure for paper and packaging rose modestly to 250 million tonnes. In contrast, both of the other products declined, reaching the same level of around 150 million tonnes in 1990.',
'The patterns became more different in the second half of the period. Paper and packaging output increased sharply from 250 million tonnes to 350 million in 2000. Wood pulp also rose, but only slightly, ending at about 160 million tonnes. Sawn wood continued to fall, reaching roughly 130 million tonnes. By the final year, paper and packaging output was more than twice that of either of the other products.',
'Dùng số gần đúng theo ảnh (230/170/130); không lấy số khác trong bài mẫu PDF. Sawn wood giảm, wood pulp giảm rồi hồi.',
'Body 1: 1980–1990. Body 2: 1990–2000.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','similar'],{'years':[1980,1990,2000],'unit':'million tonnes as labelled','approximate':True,'paper and packaging':[230,250,350],'wood pulp':[170,150,160],'sawn wood':[200,150,130]})
add(42,
'The table compares the numbers of five types of vehicle registered in Australia in 2010, 2012 and 2014, together with their percentage changes over the period.',
'Overall, registrations increased in every category. Passenger vehicles were by far the most numerous, while light trucks remained the least common. Motorcycles recorded the largest percentage increase.',
'Passenger vehicles rose from 11.8 million in 2010 to 12.7 million in 2012 and 13 million in 2014. This represented an increase of 10.2% over the four years. Commercial vehicles were the second largest group, with registrations increasing from 2.3 million to 2.6 million and then 2.7 million. Their overall growth rate was higher, at 17.4%.',
'Among the smaller categories, motorcycle registrations increased from 540,000 in 2010 to 680,000 in 2012 and 709,000 in 2014, a rise of 30.8%. Heavy trucks grew more slowly, from 384,000 to 416,000, with the smallest percentage increase of 8.3%. Light trucks rose from 106,000 to 124,000 and then 131,000. Although they remained the smallest category, their reported increase of 23.5% was second only to motorcycles.',
'Phân biệt số lượng với tốc độ tăng: passenger nhiều nhất, motorcycles tăng % mạnh nhất. % change dùng theo bảng nguồn.',
'Body 1: passenger/commercial. Body 2: motorcycle/heavy/light trucks.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','respectively'],{'years':[2010,2012,2014],'passenger':[11800000,12700000,13000000],'commercial':[2300000,2600000,2700000],'motorcycles':[540000,680000,709000],'heavy trucks':[384000,390000,416000],'light trucks':[106000,124000,131000]})
add(43,
'The maps compare the layout of Forton Valley City in 2000 and 2010.',
'Overall, farmland and a dairy farm were replaced by public and educational facilities. The area gained a university, a library and a cafe, while the shopping centre and the main roads remained in place.',
'In 2000, Sheffield Road ran along the northern side, and a second road divided the area into western and eastern sections. The shopping centre occupied the northwest corner. Below it were farmland and a dairy farm. By 2010, the shopping centre was unchanged, but the farmland had become a playground. The former dairy farm area contained a kindergarten school and a toy shop.',
'On the eastern side, the city hall was converted into a public library. The kindergarten school that had occupied the northeast corner was replaced by Forton University. The park in the southeast was removed to make way for a university cafe. The parking area beside the central road was also expanded into two sections. Despite these changes to the buildings and land use, the overall road arrangement stayed the same.',
'Bản đồ có Bắc; school cũ thành university; school mới bên tây. Không nhầm library với city hall giữ nguyên chức năng.',
'Body 1: phía tây. Body 2: phía đông.',['map-overview','map-change','location'])
add(44,
'The table shows the percentages of Australian women aged 40–44 who had different numbers of children in 1981, 1986, 1996 and 2006.',
'Overall, having two children became increasingly common and was the largest category in every year shown. The shares with no children or one child increased, whereas the proportions with three or at least four children declined.',
'In 1981, 29% of women in this age group had two children. This figure rose to 35.6% in 1986 and 38.2% in 1996, before reaching 38.3% in 2006. The percentage with no children also increased steadily, from 8.5% to 15.9% over the whole period. Similarly, the share with one child grew from 7.6% in 1981 to 13.2% in 2006.',
'Larger families showed the opposite pattern. Women with three children accounted for 27.4% in 1981, slightly below the two-child figure. Their share then fell to 27% in 1986, 24.6% in 1996 and 21.5% in 2006. The decline was much greater among women with four or more children, whose proportion dropped from 27.6% to 11%, leaving this as the smallest category in the final year.',
'Đọc theo thứ tự năm tăng dần, dù bảng in năm mới nhất trước. Đối tượng là women aged 40–44, không phải mọi phụ nữ.',
'Body 1: 0–2 children tăng. Body 2: 3 và 4+ giảm.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','similar'],{'years':[1981,1986,1996,2006],'none':[8.5,9.7,12.8,15.9],'one':[7.6,8.7,11.3,13.2],'two':[29,35.6,38.2,38.3],'three':[27.4,27,24.6,21.5],'four+':[27.6,18.9,13.1,11]})
add(45,
'The chart compares education levels among five age groups in Glasgow in 2010, showing the percentages with a university degree, a school certificate or no qualifications.',
'Overall, university degrees were the most common qualification in all groups below age 75. In contrast, most people in the oldest group had no qualifications. The proportion with a degree was highest among those aged 24–35.',
'Among 16–24-year-olds, 71% had a university degree, 20% had a school certificate and 9% had no qualifications. The 35–50 group had exactly the same distribution. For people aged 24–35, the degree figure was slightly higher, at 76%, while the school-certificate share was lower, at 15%. The remaining 9% had no qualifications.',
'The older groups showed a different pattern. Half of those aged 50–75 had a university degree, compared with 20% holding a school certificate and 30% having no qualifications. In the 75-and-over group, only 25% had a degree and 3% had a school certificate. The proportion without qualifications rose to 72%, making it by far the largest category among the oldest people shown.',
'Giữ đúng nhóm tuổi như nhãn nguồn, không tự sửa ranh giới tuổi. Đây là snapshot 2010, không nói một người mất bằng khi già.',
'Body 1: ba nhóm trẻ. Body 2: hai nhóm lớn tuổi.',['intro','static-overview','compare','respectively'],{'groups':['16–24','24–35','35–50','50–75','75+'],'degree':[71,76,71,50,25],'school':[20,15,20,20,3],'none':[9,9,9,30,72]})
add(46,
'The table compares the percentages of people aged 65 and over in Canada, Germany and the UK in 1988 and 2000, with predictions for 2030.',
'Overall, the proportion of older people increased in all three countries and is expected to rise further. Germany has the highest figure at every point shown, while the UK has the lowest.',
'In 1988, people aged at least 65 accounted for 20% of Germany’s population, compared with 16% in Canada and 14% in the UK. By 2000, the German figure had risen to 25%, an increase of five percentage points. Canada recorded the same size of increase, reaching 21%. The UK changed much less over this period, with its share growing by only one percentage point to 15%.',
'The figures for all three countries are projected to increase by a further five percentage points between 2000 and 2030. Germany is expected to reach 30%, followed by Canada at 26% and the UK at 20%. Thus, the ranking of the countries is not predicted to change, and the gap between Germany and Canada is expected to remain at four percentage points.',
'2030 là dự báo. Dữ liệu này là bản làm tròn; q048 có số thập phân, không trộn hai bản.',
'Body 1: 1988–2000. Body 2: dự báo 2030.',['intro','overview-trend','forecast','respectively'],{'years':[1988,2000,2030],'unit':'percent','Canada':[16,21,26],'Germany':[20,25,30],'UK':[14,15,20]})
hold(47,'Lời đề nói million dollars per household và trục $ million, nhưng giá trị 500–4,400 không hợp lý ở cấp hộ. Không tự đổi thành dollars khi chưa xác nhận đơn vị.')
add(48,
'The table shows the percentages of the population aged 65 and above in Canada, Germany and the UK in 1988 and 2000, together with predictions for 2030.',
'Overall, all three countries had an increasing share of older people, and further growth is predicted. Germany records the highest percentages throughout the table, while the UK remains the lowest.',
'In 1988, Germany’s figure was 20.35%, compared with 16.45% in Canada and 14.25% in the UK. By 2000, the share in Germany had increased to 25.53%. Canada also saw a clear rise, reaching 20.65%. In contrast, the UK recorded only a small change over the same period, with its figure increasing to 14.80%, still below Canada’s initial level.',
'By 2030, the German proportion is projected to reach 30.65%, the highest figure in the table. Canada is expected to follow at 26.35%, while the UK is predicted to reach 20.45%. Compared with 2000, the expected increases are roughly five to six percentage points in each country. Despite this common upward direction, the ranking is forecast to stay unchanged, with Germany ahead of Canada and the UK.',
'Giữ số thập phân chính xác theo bản này. Không chấm đáp án 26% là số chính xác của Canada 2030 trong q048.',
'Body 1: 1988 và 2000. Body 2: 2030.',['intro','overview-trend','forecast','compare'],{'years':[1988,2000,2030],'unit':'percent','Canada':[16.45,20.65,26.35],'Germany':[20.35,25.53,30.65],'UK':[14.25,14.8,20.45]})
add(49,
'The bar chart compares the populations of Jakarta, Shanghai and Sao Paulo in 1990 with the predicted and actual figures for 2000, measured in millions.',
'Overall, Sao Paulo was the largest city in both years, while Jakarta was the smallest. All three populations grew, and the actual figures for 2000 were higher than the predictions.',
'Sao Paulo had approximately 17 million residents in 1990. Its population was expected to reach around 21 million in 2000, but the actual total was closer to 24 million. It therefore remained well ahead of the other two cities. Shanghai began at about 12 million, while its predicted figure for 2000 was lower, at approximately 11 million. In fact, its population increased to around 15 million.',
'Jakarta’s population was roughly 9 million in 1990. The forecast for 2000 was approximately 11 million, but the actual figure reached about 12.5 million. This was the smallest difference between prediction and reality among the three cities. Although Jakarta and Shanghai both grew, neither approached Sao Paulo’s population, and the order of the three cities remained unchanged in the actual 2000 figures.',
'So sánh actual và prediction cho cùng năm 2000; không coi prediction là năm trung gian. Số đọc gần đúng.',
'Body 1: Sao Paulo–Shanghai. Body 2: Jakarta và so sánh sai lệch.',['intro','compare','from-to'],{'unit':'million people','approximate':True,'Jakarta':{'1990':9,'2000 predicted':11,'2000 actual':12.5},'Shanghai':{'1990':12,'2000 predicted':11,'2000 actual':15},'Sao Paulo':{'1990':17,'2000 predicted':21,'2000 actual':24}})
